es-up-high">17. Matching Baskets and Supplies Up High</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#18-a-drip-pan-and-a-leak-sensor">18. A Drip Pan and a Leak Sensor</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#laundry-closet-mistakes-to-avoid">Laundry Closet Mistakes to Avoid</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#laundry-closet-faq">Laundry Closet FAQ</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-much-space-do-you-need-for-a-laundry-closet">How much space do you need for a laundry closet?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#can-you-put-a-washer-and-dryer-in-a-closet">Can you put a washer and dryer in a closet?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#do-laundry-closet-doors-need-to-be-louvered">Do laundry closet doors need to be louvered?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-i-make-a-hallway-laundry-closet-look-nicer">How do I make a hallway laundry closet look nicer?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-you-hide-a-washer-and-dryer-in-a-hallway">How do you hide a washer and dryer in a hallway?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#can-you-put-a-washer-and-dryer-in-a-bathroom">Can you put a washer and dryer in a bathroom?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-you-hide-a-washer-and-dryer-in-a-kitchen">How do you hide a washer and dryer in a kitchen?</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#final-thoughts">Final Thoughts</a></li></ul></div></nav>


<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How Much Space Does a Laundry Closet Need?</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Before you buy shelves or doors, measure the inside of the closet: width, depth and height. Then compare those numbers with the machines you have or plan to buy. Whirlpool’s <a href="https://www.whirlpool.com/blog/washers-and-dryers/laundry-sizing-guide.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">laundry sizing guide</a> lists typical full-size front-loaders at about 27 inches wide, 39 inches high and 32 to 34 inches deep, and compact models at about 24 inches wide. It recommends about 1 inch of space on each side and 6 inches behind the machines for ventilation and hose connections, and it reminds you to check that closet doors can open and close fully.</p>



